  m_Name: Shack4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Question
  questionText: "Why haven\u2019t you switched the power back off yet?"
  largeQuestionBox: 0
  conversation:
  - <i>...Oh my God.</i>
  - Not that simple.
  - "The system gets messed up when it isn\u2019t shut off the proper way."
  - "So since the power wasn\u2019t \u2018turned off,\u2019 the system\u2019s been
    fried, so I have a lot to fix. i.e., you should <i>leave</i>."
  - ...
  - ...
  - ...no?
  - I mean, so what are you saying then?
  - "That I\u2019m too lazy to throw one switch?"
  - "I don\u2019t have any reason for <i>wanting</i> the power kept on, so what is
    it that you\u2019re still trying to say?"
  - "No, that\u2019s..."
  - ...
  - "That\u2019s the entire picture."
  - "I\u2019m into gore."
  - '[MASK SHATTERS]'
  - '!...'
  - ...
  - "You\u2019re only here for the one murder, right?"
  - Because there's about to be another one.
  - ...Goddamn, fine. <i>Fine!</i>
  - "Every morning I get up at 5 to start a download, because it literally takes
    all day to load one goddamn picture. That\u2019s how bad the internet is here."
  - "So when I found that the power had been switched off, yeah, I figured it had
    been Fishburn. He\u2019s done it before, but he usually does it at night so I
    don\u2019t really care."
  - "Anyway I didn\u2019t know about old Mr BBQ up on the lines, so I just turned
    it right back on."
  - "God, couldn\u2019t you have just waited 9 more hours?!"
  - "Just...just <i>get out of here</i> and I\u2019ll turn the damn power off."
  - "God, <i>I</i> ask for half-decent internet, but apparently 'That\u2019s just
    not a priority!'"
  - No, apparently a <i>real</i> priority, is a <i>second fucking squash court.</i>
